Upgrading to Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL
======================================

When Neon free tier limits become a constraint (storage, availability, cold
starts), upgrade to Cloud SQL. The only change is the DATABASE_URL secret and
adding a Cloud SQL connection flag to the deploy command.

1. Enable Cloud SQL Admin API
-----------------------------
    gcloud services enable sqladmin.googleapis.com

2. Create a Cloud SQL instance
------------------------------
    gcloud sql instances create volunteer-call-db \
      --database-version=POSTGRES_16 \
      --tier=db-f1-micro \
      --region=us-central1 \
      --storage-size=10GB \
      --storage-auto-increase

db-f1-micro is ~$10/month. For lower cost during development, stop the
instance when not in use:

    gcloud sql instances patch volunteer-call-db --activation-policy=NEVER   # stop
    gcloud sql instances patch volunteer-call-db --activation-policy=ALWAYS  # start

3. Create database and user
---------------------------
    gcloud sql databases create volunteer_call --instance=volunteer-call-db

    gcloud sql users create volunteer_call_user \
      --instance=volunteer-call-db \
      --password=<generate-a-strong-password>

4. Update DATABASE_URL in Secret Manager
----------------------------------------
Cloud SQL connection string uses the instance connection name (not a hostname):

    PROJECT=$(gcloud config get-value project)
    CONN_NAME="${PROJECT}:us-central1:volunteer-call-db"

    # The app connects via Cloud SQL Auth Proxy built into Cloud Run
    DATABASE_URL="postgresql+asyncpg://volunteer_call_user:<password>@/volunteer_call?host=/cloudsql/${CONN_NAME}"

    echo -n "$DATABASE_URL" | \
      gcloud secrets versions add volunteer-call-database-url --data-file=-

5. Update Cloud Run deploy command
-----------------------------------
Add the --add-cloudsql-instances flag. In the Makefile deploy target or
.github/workflows/deploy.yml, add:

    --add-cloudsql-instances=$(PROJECT):us-central1:volunteer-call-db

6. Grant Cloud SQL access to Cloud Run service account
------------------------------------------------------
The runtime service account (created by `scripts/set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy`)
needs `roles/cloudsql.client`:

    PROJECT=$(gcloud config get-value project)
    RUNTIME_SA="volunteer-call-runtime@${PROJECT}.iam.gserviceaccount.com"

    gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding "$PROJECT" \
      --member="serviceAccount:${RUNTIME_SA}" \
      --role="roles/cloudsql.client"

(If you fall back to the default Compute Engine service account instead of a
dedicated runtime SA, substitute `${PROJECT_NUMBER}-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com`.)

7. Seed data via cloud-sql-proxy
---------------------------------
Install the proxy: https://cloud.google.com/sql/docs/postgres/sql-proxy

    # Terminal 1: start proxy
    cloud-sql-proxy ${PROJECT}:us-central1:volunteer-call-db --port=5433

    # Terminal 2: seed
    export DATABASE_URL='postgresql://volunteer_call_user:<password>@localhost:5433/volunteer_call'
    psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f scripts/initdb/01-schema.sql
    psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f scripts/initdb/02-reference-data.sql

8. Cost reference
-----------------
- db-f1-micro: ~$10/month (shared CPU, 614 MB RAM)
- db-g1-small: ~$26/month (shared CPU, 1.7 GB RAM)
- Storage: $0.17/GB/month
- Stop instance when not in use to avoid compute charges
- See https://cloud.google.com/sql/pricing for current rates
